 "result": "\n\nSaved `scenario.json` for `G4-SLK-05`.\n\n**Request:** \"In my DM with Diego Alvarez, add a raised-hands reaction to the message he posted about the Meridian invoice deadline.\"\n\nThe record acted on is Diego's message in the actor's 1:1 DM with him. Conditions: in my DM (`A:Conversation.is_dm`) / with Diego Alvarez (`R:channel_members`) / the message he posted (`R:messages.user_id`) / about the Meridian invoice deadline (`A:Message.message_text`). All four decoys carry Diego's own message containing the same \"Meridian invoice deadline\" wording, so each fails only the is_dm condition:\n\n| Decoys (fact `A:Conversation.is_dm`, all via DROP of the is_dm filter) |\n|---|\n| **F7** — `@msg_group`: Diego posts the same message in a three-person **group DM** (actor + Diego + Aisha) — the nearest conversation kind on the wrong side of a 1:1 DM (the replica reports it as private, making it extra tempting). |\n| **F1** — `@msg_priv`: Diego posts it in the **private `#vendors` channel** — the sibling privacy flag (`is_private`) set instead of the DM flag. |\n| **F0** — `@msg_pub`: Diego posts it in the **public `#finance` channel** — plainly the wrong kind of conversation. |\n\nBackground messages (Aisha in the group DM and `#finance`, Omar in `#vendors`) each fail three conditions, so they never compete with the decoys.",
